https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=KkI-7F0ks0c  (Capo 0) (MC0)

There’s also a version by the Dubliners.

TIP:  Three versions available.  This one in (C) to play along with the recording by The Seekers.  But while I prefer the musical arrangement of the Seekers I prefer the more traditional lyrics in the Dubliner’s version as it’s more complete.  So there’s also a hybrid version, one in (C) and one in (G), keeping the Seeker’s music but with the Dubliner’s lyrics.

TIP:  Assuming it even has one and it’s not just a musical convenience, the most accepted, albeit speculative, Gaelic meaning attributed to the chorus is “musha ringum duram do” means “whiskey for the fool” and “whack fol the daddy-o” is “in memory of my father.”  
   

